      "writtenOn": "2024-02-27T03:38:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll leave it up to Remi...\n\nbut... personally I think:\n\n(a) this is a *lot* of complexity\n\n(a1) The performance of Struct.java is kind of critical to the performance of our code.\nThe arch-ness of userspace/kernel should be figured out *once* in some Struct singleton class, and then padding should be adjusted during Struct class creation (ie. once per Class instance) and not constantly...\n\n(a2) It seems a bit pointless to add this for a single use case...\n\nespecially since we now have VTS tests that block x86 32-bit kernels, and indeed even bpfloader (which is mainlined, and thus not normally mutable by oem/vendor) does:\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Connectivity/netbpfload/NetBpfLoad.cpp;drc\u003d7f6a42672ddbd8910a63c344c1882a554cef241c;l\u003d304\n\nif (isAtLeastV \u0026\u0026 android::bpf::isX86() \u0026\u0026 !android::bpf::isKernel64Bit()) {\n        ALOGE(\"Android V requires X86 kernel to be 64-bit.\");\n        return 1;\n        \nwhich means V+ can\u0027t hit a 32-bit x86 kernel.\n\n(b) this isn\u0027t enough complexity: as is, it doesn\u0027t actually work...\n\nThere aren\u0027t 5 supported archs - there\u0027s actually in practice 7...:\n  (arm,x86,riscv) x (32 vs 64-bit kernel) x (32 vs 64-bit userspace)\nof these 3*2*2\u003d12, some combinations are invalid:\n- we don\u0027t support 32-bit riscV (- 3)\n- can\u0027t run 64-bit userspace on a 32-bit kernel (- 2)\nthus 12 - 3 - 2 \u003d 7\n\nAdditionally layout may depend on the actual version of the kernel,\nie. 4.9 vs 4.14, possibly even the LTS version, or even if it is an ACK kernel or a non-ACK Linux kernel.\n\nThere were some \u0027just fail the api if 32-bit userspace tries to use it on a 64-bit kernel\u0027 upstream that were reverted in Android kernels...\n\nThere were some fixes that landed upstream only in newer kernels to add compat code for struct layouts (so 32-bit userspace on a 64-bit kernel would behave like on a 32-bit kernel)... that we then reverted in Android, so our newer kernels would behave the same as older ones...\n\nIn general there\u0027s a moratorium on 32-bit kernels even with arm for new launch devices on U+, so 32-bit is almost dead...\n\n(there\u0027s VTS tests for this on newer kernel versions like 6.2+ or something)\n\n---\n\nAs such I think I\u0027d prefer to just not support this...",
      "revId": "df3a4d56d60959aae081418fd5e210bc538d5c08",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
