      "writtenOn": "2024-03-04T11:01:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If x86_32 isn\u0027t actually supported by other parts of the system, I guess the structs shouldn\u0027t need to worry about it. And aosp/2912434 only needs a different padding for that architecture, so maybe we don\u0027t need this change at all in that case ?\n\nWe may want to land it later when we have other structs that need this though; in which case we\u0027d need to address Maze\u0027s comment b) about the arch not being enough (maybe one way would be to have some per-struct list of formats that don\u0027t necessarily map 1:1 with architectures, with some static getter in the struct to define the format to use ?).\n\nBut maybe we don\u0027t need to merge this until the use-case is here then ?",
      "parentUuid": "680c0e92_7a5db591",
      "revId": "df3a4d56d60959aae081418fd5e210bc538d5c08",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
